# Reference only: do NOT copy this to .env or .env.local. Expo loads .env files into the dev
# server and has logged their values. Set these in the server's process environment instead
# (your shell or OS user environment locally, secret environment variables in EAS Hosting).
# Variables without the EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix are only read by server code (API routes in
# src/app/api) and are never bundled into the app.

# Which AI provider the API routes call: "anthropic" or "openrouter". Without it, OpenRouter is
# used only when OPENROUTER_API_KEY is the sole key set; otherwise Anthropic.
# TRUSTGUARD_AI_PROVIDER=openrouter

# Anthropic key (sk-ant-...), from https://platform.claude.com/
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter key (sk-or-...), from https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Requests use OpenRouter's Anthropic-compatible Messages endpoint and are routed only to
# Anthropic itself. A key is only ever sent to the provider that issued it: an OpenRouter key in
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (or the reverse) is refused and AI features stay off.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Claude model, in the selected provider's naming.
# Defaults: claude-opus-5-5 (Anthropic), anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 (OpenRouter).
# Non-Claude models are refused: the analyzers rely on Claude's structured outputs, web search
# tool and citations, and vision.
# TRUSTGUARD_CLAIM_MODEL=

# Optional: absolute URL of a deployed backend. Leave empty to use relative URLs
# (the Expo dev server in development, the expo-router `origin` in production builds).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=
